            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s46",
                "printed_page": "5",
                "text": "וְהַעֲרֶב־נָא יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ אֶת דִּבְרֵי תוֹרָתְךָ בְּפִינוּ וּבְפִי עַמְּךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל וְנִהְיֶה אֲנַחְנוּ וְצֶאֱצָאֵינוּ וְצֶאֱצָאֵי עַמְּךָ בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל כֻּלָּנוּ יוֹדְעֵי שְׁמֶךָ וְלוֹמְדֵי תוֹרָתֶךָ (לִשְׁמָהּ). בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְיָ הַמְלַמֵּד תּוֹרָה לְעַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל:"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s47",
                "printed_page": "5",
                "text": "And so, O Lord our God, let the words of Thy Torah be pleasing in our mouth and in the mouth of Thy people the House of Israel so that we and our descendants and the descendants of Thy people the House of Israel may all acknowledge Thy Name and learn Thy Torah (with pure intent). Blessed art Thou, O Lord, who teaches the Torah to His people Israel ."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
